---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Ref from '../components/Ref.astro';
import { actBy } from '../lib/site';

const last = actBy(5);
---

<Base
  title="Is Stranger Than Heaven a Yakuza Game? The Like a Dragon Link"
  description="Stranger Than Heaven shares its world with Like a Dragon (Yakuza) but is a separate game. What the developers say about Kamurocho and the Tojo Clan."
  path="/like-a-dragon-connection/"
>
  <h1>Is Stranger Than Heaven a Yakuza game?</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Short answer: it is made by the same studio and set in the same fictional world as Like a Dragon, the series once
    called Yakuza in the West. It is sold as its own game, not as an entry in that series
    <Ref ids="automaton" />.
  </p>

  <h2>What ties the two together</h2>
  <ul class="prose">
    <li>
      <strong>The studio.</strong> RGG Studio, the SEGA team behind Like a Dragon, develops it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The world.</strong> Studio head Masayoshi Yokoyama has said the game takes place in the Like a Dragon
      world, while calling it a separate title <Ref ids="automaton" />.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Kamurocho.</strong> The last act, in {last.year}, is set in Kamurocho, the fictional Shinjuku district
      where most Like a Dragon games take place <Ref ids="sega-0925" />.
      <a href={`/acts/${last.slug}/`}>More on Act 5</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The Tojo Clan.</strong> According to Yokoyama, the place Makoto Daito sets out to build for himself
      grows, in time, into the Tojo Clan, the yakuza organisation at the centre of the series
      <Ref ids="automaton" />.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>A familiar voice.</strong> Takaya Kuroda, the voice of Kazuma Kiryu, plays a craftsman called Takeo
      Godai <Ref ids="sega-0925" />. <a href="/cast/">See the full cast</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Why it is not called Like a Dragon</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Yokoyama's explanation is that it plays differently. There is no cabaret club and no karaoke, and the controls
      and the way your character grows are not the ones series players know, so putting the Like a Dragon name on the
      box would mislead people <Ref ids="automaton" />.
    </p>
    <p>
      Fighting is one example: each of Makoto's arms has its own buttons. Show business is another: you write songs
      and stage shows. Both are covered on the <a href="/gameplay/">gameplay page</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Where it sits in the timeline</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      The story runs from 1915 to 1965. Yakuza 0, the earliest story in the main series, is set in 1988, so this one
      ends more than twenty years before that one begins. The five eras are laid out on the
      <a href="/acts/">acts page</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>How long is it?</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      No hour count has been given. In the same interview Yokoyama described the game as "frankly, long", with a
      great deal in it <Ref ids="automaton" />. The <a href="/achievements/">achievement list</a> points the same way:
      five acts, substories in every city and a show business story running alongside.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
